# jemdoc: menu{MENU_topics}{topics.html}
= Research (By Topic)

My research focuses on the design and deployment of AI systems that empower human decision-makers and improve societal outcomes. Operating at the intersection of machine learning, operations research, and economics, I investigate the complex dynamics of human-AI interaction. To bridge theory and practice, I develop novel methodologies in contextual bandits, transfer learning, and policy optimization, and rigorously test these approaches through large-scale field deployments in healthcare, education, and public policy. Selected papers in each direction (1) [/topics.html\#ai-for-social-impact AI for social impact], (2) [/topics.html\#algos ML/AI Algorithmic Methods], and (3) [/topics.html\#human-ai human-AI collaboration] are included below.

{{<span id="ai-for-social-impact" class="section-anchor"></span>}}
== AI for Social Impact

I am especially excited about partnering with governments, NGOs, and schools to study how/where AI can improve human outcomes in the field.

